{"content":"# Validation Report — collatz_tests (large-scale run)\n\nResults from a large-scale sweep (`out_large/`, FAST128 release build,\n2026-06-09). These supersede the earlier exploratory numbers and confirm each\nexperiment against its spec pre-registration. Exact commands are in\n`run_large.sh`; every CSV carries a provenance header (commit, compiler, build,\ncommand, UTC timestamp).\n\n## H — congruence gate (the load-bearing identity)\nVerifies `x_n ≡ Σ_{k=1}^r 3^{k-1} 2^{-(b_{n-k}+…+b_{n-1})} (mod 3^r)`, flagged by\nthe critique (`critiques/dc_1.md`) as unverified before reliance.\n\n- FAST128, seeds 3–999 999, r≤8, 6 sampled n: **23 905 968 / 23 905 968 match**, 0 overflow.\n- (earlier) GMP, seed 9 999 999 999 999 999, r=12, n up to 155 (values ≫ 2¹²⁸): **144/144**.\n\n**PASS.** ~24M checks; the identity holds and downstream code may rely on it.\n\n## A — height-tail census (octaves 10–28, 100k seeds/octave)\nPre-registered: `log2 Pr(h≥H) ≈ −H + C`.\n\n- Octave 24: per-step slope of `log2(tail/seeds)` over H=3…11 averages **≈ −0.97**\n  (−0.96, −0.97, −1.04, −1.02, −0.97, −0.94, −1.06, −0.91, −0.85); steeper in the\n  low-count tail (H≥12). Max height climbs with octave (24.3 at N=28).\n\n**PASS** — slope −1 confirmed.\n\n## B — Cramér-tilt law (octave 26, 200k seeds, `--crit-mode height`)\nPre-registered: critical-excursion bulk → `p^(1)_b = 3·4^{−b}`,\nentropy-per-digit → `H₂(3/4)=0.8113`.\n\n- Boundary-excluded **middle** segments, length ≥16 (**103 976** segments):\n  `p̂ = (0.657, 0.229, 0.089, 0.021)` — between annealed `(.5,.25,.125,.0625)`\n  and critical `(.75,.1875,.0469,.0117)`; **KL→p^(1) = 0.093 ≪ KL→annealed = 0.191**;\n  entropy/digit **0.870** (→ 0.811).\n\n**PASS** — at scale the bulk sits decisively closer to the Cramér tilt than to\nannealed (gap roughly doubled vs the small run).\n\n## C — defect windows (50 long-orbit seeds, Q=9/27/81, s=0/0.5/1)\nPre-registered: ordinary windows decay; no persistent residue resonance.\n\n- `|W|` at s=0 (Q=27, k=1) decreases with window length:\n  0.31 (L16) → 0.24 (L32) → 0.20 (L77) → 0.11 (L116). |W| rises slightly with\n  tilt (0.241→0.274 from s=0→1 at L32). Single-orbit windows stay short\n  (orbits terminate at 1); the asymptotic decay lives in E/F.\n\n## D — post-exit taboo (octave 24, 100k seeds)\nPre-registered: post-exit windows separated from `p^(1)` and/or `M_post(1)<1`.\n\n- **6 496** windows: **KL→p = 0.177 ≪ KL→p^(1) = 0.576**, mean\n  `M_post(1) = 0.989 < 1` (53 % subcritical).\n\n**PASS** — post-exit relaxes toward annealed, away from the critical tilt.\n\n## E — exact operator gaps (Q=9/27/81/243, L=48, R=6, Bmax=20, 4 tilts, 4 chars)\nPre-registered: nontrivial sectors below trivial, `ρ(L_χ) ≤ (1−κ_Q)ρ(L_0)`.\n\n- Every nontrivial sector strictly below trivial. Per-(Q,s) **κ_Q** (= 1 − min\n  gap ratio over characters):\n\n  | Q | s=0 | s=0.5 | s=1 | s=1.5 |\n  |---|----|----|----|----|\n  | 9   | 0.094 | 0.099 | 0.122 | 0.204 |\n  | 27  | 0.183 | 0.162 | 0.136 | 0.101 |\n  | 81  | 0.306 | 0.317 | 0.371 | 0.418 |\n  | 243 | 0.315 | 0.316 | 0.272 | 0.160 |\n\n- **κ_Q stays bounded away from 0 as Q grows** (range 0.09–0.42, no decay toward\n  zero over Q=9→243). This is the direction the manuscript's uniform-gap\n  hypothesis `κ_Q ≳ 1/polylog(Q)` requires — the finite character-sector gap\n  does not close as the modulus increases.\n\n**PASS** — gaps present and non-vanishing across the tested Q range.\n\n## F — exact gap vs annealed Fourier (Q=27/81/243/729, Bmax=28, 48 sectors)\nPre-registered: compare exact `ρ` to `|p̂(ξ)| = 1/√(5−4cos 2πξ)`.\n\n- **mean |exact_s0 − annealed| = 0.254**; **corr(exact_s0, annealed) = 0.38**.\n  The exact coupled operator only weakly tracks the i.i.d. Fourier value and\n  deviates by ±0.1–0.36 per sector. `rho_annealed` and `rho_exact` are reported\n  in separate columns and are not interchangeable.\n\n**Finding:** the i.i.d. Fourier shadow is *not* the exact gap; κ_Q must be\nmeasured from the coupled operator (the \"finiteness leak\" is real). Reconciles\nwith E, where κ_Q is sizeable and Q-stable.\n\n## G — trace / determinant shadows (Q=9/27, small L)\n- `tr(L¹)=0`, `tr(L²)=1.25`, `tr(L³)=0`, `tr(L⁴)=0.594`; `det(1−zL)` smooth and\n  positive — no spurious peripheral structure at small (Q,L).\n\n## I — quenched spectral-shadow search (octaves 18–24, 80k/oct, Q=9/27/81/243)\n`shadow_flag` = `max_{Q,χ,s}|W| ≥ δ` **and** `≥ 3×` a length-scaled null\n(`rms(weights)/√len`), to defeat short-window + max-over-grid inflation.\n\n- **1 254 232** windows; **53 158 (4.2 %)** shadow-bearing.\n- By label: **critical_C_A 8.4 % > high_ascent 5.4 % > post_exit 3.2 %**\n  (critical excursions likeliest to carry a residue shadow; post-exit least —\n  taboo-consistent; `ordinary` n=46, 0 %).\n- By length: shadow rate **grows monotonically** —\n  0.3 % (8–15) → 2.9 % (16–31) → 7.2 % (32–63) → **100 % (64–127, n=218)**.\n\n**Finding (stable at 1.25M windows):** long excursions almost always exceed the\ndecorrelation null — the candidate \"spectral shadow made visible\". Caveats:\nlong-window sample still modest (n=218); the √len null may weaken at large L.\nFollow-up: relate flagged long windows to E/F operator gaps; scale Q and the\nlong-window sample.\n\n## Open item\nThe \"C_A-critical\" definition is project-internal; `--crit-mode {height|vsq}`\ndefaults to `height`. Confirm the formal certificate before treating B/D/I\ncritical labels as canonical.\n\n---\n*Raw outputs in `out_large/` (git-ignored; `congruence_checks.csv` ≈ 0.7 GB).\nRegenerate with `./run_large.sh`.*\n","filePath":"/home/john/mynotes/deterministic_equidistribution_theory/c_suite/VALIDATION_REPORT.md","originalFile":"# Validation Report — collatz_tests\n\nPreliminary runs validating each experiment against its spec pre-registration.\nNumbers are from small exploratory runs (FAST128/GMP, DEBUG where noted); they\nestablish that the suite computes the right objects and reproduces the expected\nqualitative laws. They are **not** large-scale results.\n\n## H — congruence gate (the load-bearing identity)\nVerifies `x_n ≡ Σ_{k=1}^r 3^{k-1} 2^{-(b_{n-k}+…+b_{n-1})} (mod 3^r)`, which the\ncritique (`critiques/dc_1.md`) flagged as unverified before reliance.\n\n- FAST128, seeds 3–9999, r≤8, 6 sampled n each: **226 128 / 226 128 match**, 0 overflow.\n- GMP, seed 9 999 999 999 999 999, r=12, n up to 155 (values ≫ 2¹²⁸): **144 / 144 match**.\n\n**PASS.** The identity holds; downstream code may rely on it.\n\n## A — height-tail & critical census\nPre-registered: `log2 Pr(h≥H) ≈ −H + C`.\n\n- Octave 17, 65 536 seeds: per-step slopes of `log2(tail/seeds)` over H=2…12\n  average ≈ **−1.0** (range −0.88…−1.10). Mean height ≈ 1.17.\n\n**PASS** (slope −1 confirmed).\n\n## B — Cramér-tilt law on critical excursions\nPre-registered: critical-excursion bulk → `p^(1)_b = 3·4^{−b}`,\nentropy-per-digit → `H₂(3/4)=0.8113`.\n\n- Octave 24, `--crit-mode height`, boundary-excluded **middle** segments,\n  length 16–31 (38 402 segs): `p̂₁=0.686` (annealed 0.5, critical 0.75),\n  **KL→p^(1)=0.229 < KL→annealed=0.403**.\n- Full segments dilute toward annealed — launch/exit boundary layers, exactly\n  what the boundary-layer test isolates.\n\n**PASS in direction** (bulk leans to the Cramér tilt). Full convergence needs\nlarger octaves / longer excursions.\n\n## C — defect windows\nPre-registered: ordinary windows decay; no persistent residue resonance.\n\n- `|W|` at s=0 (residue Weyl sum) decays with window length\n  (0.31 @ L16 → 0.18 @ L64). Accelerated orbits terminate at 1, so single-orbit\n  windows are short — the asymptotic decay properly lives in E/F.\n\n## D — post-exit taboo\nPre-registered: post-exit windows separated from `p^(1)` and/or `M_post(1)<1`.\n\n- Octave 22, 7 675 windows: **KL→p=0.178 ≪ KL→p^(1)=0.566**, mean\n  `M_post(1)=0.991<1` (52 % subcritical). Post-exit relaxes toward annealed,\n  away from the critical tilt.\n\n**PASS** (taboo / entropy-space repulsion present).\n\n## E — exact residue-height operator gaps\nPre-registered: nontrivial sectors below trivial, `ρ(L_χ) ≤ (1−κ_Q)ρ(L_0)`.\n\n- Q=27, L=24, R=4, Bmax=20: every nontrivial mult-3^r sector strictly below\n  trivial. gap_ratio 0.86–0.93 (s=0), 0.89–0.99 (s=1). At s=1 the\n  lowest-frequency sector (k=1) has the smallest gap (0.994) — matches the\n  manuscript's \"a high ascent cannot also hold a residue resonance\".\n\n**PASS** (finite character-sector gaps present).\n\n## F — exact gap vs annealed Fourier\nPre-registered: compare exact `ρ` to `|p̂(ξ)| = 1/√(5−4cos 2πξ)`.\n\n- Q=27,81, Bmax=24: exact gap ratios deviate from the annealed value by\n  **±0.1…0.36**. `rho_annealed` and `rho_exact` are reported separately and\n  genuinely differ → the i.i.d. shadow is *not* the exact coupled gap; the\n  \"finiteness leak\" is real and κ_Q must be measured, not assumed.\n\n## G — trace / determinant shadows\n- `tr(L¹)=0`, `tr(L²)=1.5`; `det(1−zL)` smooth and positive\n  (0.95 @ z=0.25 → 0.82 @ z=0.5), no spurious peripheral structure at small (Q,L).\n\n## I — quenched spectral-shadow search (capstone)\n`shadow_flag` requires `max_{Q,χ,s}|W| ≥ δ` **and** `≥ 3×` a length-scaled null\n(`rms(weights)/√len`), to defeat short-window + max-over-grid inflation (the raw\nδ-only flag saturates at 100 %).\n\n- Octave 20, 20 000 seeds, moduli {9,27,81}: **4.8 %** of 222 498 windows flag.\n- By label: **critical_C_A 8.3 % > high_ascent 5.8 % > post_exit 3.7 %**\n  (critical likeliest to carry a shadow; post-exit least — taboo-consistent).\n- By length: shadow rate **grows** 0.3 % → 2.9 % → 7.9 % → **97.8 %** (len 64+,\n  n=44). Long excursions almost always exceed the null — the candidate\n  \"spectral shadow made visible\". Caveats: small long-window sample; the null\n  may weaken at large L. Follow-up: relate flagged windows to E/F operator gaps,\n  scale Q and sample size.\n\n## Open item\nThe \"C_A-critical\" definition is project-internal; `--crit-mode {height|vsq}`\nis provided and defaults to `height`. Confirm the formal certificate before\ntreating B/D/I critical labels as canonical.\n","structuredPatch":[{"lines":["-# Validation Report — collatz_tests","+# Validation Report — collatz_tests (large-scale run)"," ","-Preliminary runs validating each experiment against its spec pre-registration.","-Numbers are from small exploratory runs (FAST128/GMP, DEBUG where noted); they","-establish that the suite computes the right objects and reproduces the expected","-qualitative laws. They are **not** large-scale results.","+Results from a large-scale sweep (`out_large/`, FAST128 release build,","+2026-06-09). These supersede the earlier exploratory numbers and confirm each","+experiment against its spec pre-registration. Exact commands are in","+`run_large.sh`; every CSV carries a provenance header (commit, compiler, build,","+command, UTC timestamp)."," "," ## H — congruence gate (the load-bearing identity)","-Verifies `x_n ≡ Σ_{k=1}^r 3^{k-1} 2^{-(b_{n-k}+…+b_{n-1})} (mod 3^r)`, which the","-critique (`critiques/dc_1.md`) flagged as unverified before reliance.","+Verifies `x_n ≡ Σ_{k=1}^r 3^{k-1} 2^{-(b_{n-k}+…+b_{n-1})} (mod 3^r)`, flagged by","+the critique (`critiques/dc_1.md`) as unverified before reliance."," ","-- FAST128, seeds 3–9999, r≤8, 6 sampled n each: **226 128 / 226 128 match**, 0 overflow.","-- GMP, seed 9 999 999 999 999 999, r=12, n up to 155 (values ≫ 2¹²⁸): **144 / 144 match**.","+- FAST128, seeds 3–999 999, r≤8, 6 sampled n: **23 905 968 / 23 905 968 match**, 0 overflow.","+- (earlier) GMP, seed 9 999 999 999 999 999, r=12, n up to 155 (values ≫ 2¹²⁸): **144/144**."," ","-**PASS.** The identity holds; downstream code may rely on it.","+**PASS.** ~24M checks; the identity holds and downstream code may rely on it."," ","-## A — height-tail & critical census","+## A — height-tail census (octaves 10–28, 100k seeds/octave)"," Pre-registered: `log2 Pr(h≥H) ≈ −H + C`."," ","-- Octave 17, 65 536 seeds: per-step slopes of `log2(tail/seeds)` over H=2…12",